notes.content:
New:
- Constructor: Each question now has a slider to adjust the time to solve it, ranging from 1 to 30 seconds;
- New shaders for the existing characters, now featuring more vibrant and vivid colors;
- Settings are now stored in a file that is shared between different devices and synced using the Steam cloud;
- The host can now set the button cooldown timer, preventing players from spamming the button too frequently or cheating by using console commands;
- The host can now change the game's music (in addition to SFX).

Fixes:
- The German localization has been improved (Credits: JoKre);
- Various quality of life fixes and improvements.

- We've added translations for the camera control buttons, making it more accessible (Thanks: Osman);
- In the final round topic presentation, you'll notice a smoother experience as the cells now roll out one by one;
- We've addressed the issue where users sometimes felt that their button presses weren't properly registered. You should no longer encounter this problem;
- Lastly, we've made some camera and visual updates to enhance your overall experience

- Now, when you're scrolling down the settings menu, it won't prevent you from selecting one of the settings tabs;
- We've enhanced the usability of multiple choice questions. You can now switch between the input fields by using the Tab key;
- You can now replay audio questions without any issues;
- When you change the localization language, the selected voice will now change properly to match it;
- We've added a 'Control game' button to the navigation panel, right alongside the 'settings' button;
- Now, whenever you open any UI window such as the round change, points change, or settings, the game will pause automatically (Thanks: Alex);
- Short answers from players will now be displayed for at least 1.5 seconds. We noticed they were disappearing too quickly before;
- We've also fixed several issues related to Multiple Choice and Cat In Poke;
- If a player answers incorrectly, you'll notice a visual change in the stand – it becomes transparent.

We hope these changes enhance your gaming experience!

Game:
- Introducing a new question type (Multiple selection question);
- The current state of the game (main menu/constructor/playing) is now displayed in the Steam friends widget.

Misc:
- Added a new setting in the game settings menu, allowing only the host to select questions (Thanks: Alex);
- Introduced a punishment slider, allowing the host to reduce the number of points deducted for a wrong answer;
- An 'X' icon is now displayed beside the player stand when the player cannot answer or when the time window is closed;
- The 'greetings' and 'thank you for your support' screens are now properly displayed;
- Various localization fixes and improvements;
- Options in the game settings menu are now categorized into blocks;
- New options in the settings menu are marked to distinguish them from the old ones.

New:
- The smart camera feature is now optional; you can set it back as the default in the settings  (Thanks: Dingo);
- The remaining time window for players to join the answering queue is now visible in the UI;
- You can now randomly transfer a "cat in a poke" by clicking the button at the top;
- The host will now verbally announce the name of the player who will be answering a "cat in a poke".

Fixes:
- The smart camera has been adjusted slightly to prevent avatars from being cut off  (Thanks: Dingo);
- A bug where only the first video with sound played has been resolved (Thanks: KleinerAlsDrei);
- A bug where the music repeated after the first button press has been fixed.

Gameplay:
- The game now supports up to 10 players, including the host (previously 9);
- A theme description board is present, letting people know what is required of them when a question has already been selected;
- If you changed a round during the game using the 'control game' panel, the gameplay progression now works fine (previously broken);
- Not every player can select the question at the beginning of the game now;
- Player kick during the final round and then appearing underground has been fixed;
- The "Focus on question" camera has been improved: it won't switch back to the Overall camera during a question (previously it wasn't switching back to the Overall camera at all);
- The smart camera, depending on the number of players: it won't display the whole studio if there are only a few players playing;
- New transparent material for unoccupied stands.

Constructor:
- There's now a warning for questions with the same media used (there should be only one instance of it).

Resolved:
- The issue where selecting the same question multiple times was possible;
- The question status (whether it had been chosen or not) was not synchronized across all players and the host (Thanks: Episkbo);
- Problem, preventing players from replaying audio or skipping a question when a "cat in poke" question was active;
- Various issues with the 'replay audio' function;
- The "Time is up" prompt will no longer interrupt players while they are providing an answer;
- The display of answers when the auction cannot be played due to players having insufficient points;
- Audio-related issues associated with the continuation of questions;
- Several adjustments to input fields were made in the constructor to enhance functionality.

Constructor:
- We've added the Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y support, allowing you to undo or redo your last change;
- A new 'Try fix errors' button is now available, enabling you to quickly attempt to remove errors from your pack. Please note that every topic that exceeds the round's limit and every question that exceeds the topic's limit will be removed.

Game:
- The game's UI has undergone a complete rework. If you encounter any issues or bugs with the user interface while playing, please report them;
- New avatars have been added, while some were removed. Continue selecting avatars you prefer, as this will help us determine your favorites;
- The player who selects the question can now do so without having to inform the host verbally.

Constructor:
- The 'Tab' key now functions in the constructor, allowing you to switch between input fields;
- A skippable notification has been added to remind you to set an image for your pack when uploading it on Steam;

Game:
- The 'overall' camera now functions correctly when the 'focus on question' mode is selected;
- Fixed several bugs related to kicking players out of the game;
- Added additional lines for a cat in a poke/auction question when there's only one player playing;
- The host can no longer select two questions simultaneously, bugging the game out (thanks: S1LLE);
- A new players stand has been added;

Menu:
- A filter menu is now available, allowing you to filter packs by their language, difficulty, or category;
- The pause menu now closes properly.

- The anti-profanity filter is now online;
(Slurs are replaced with ***)
- The Auto-Reconnect feature has been enabled;
(Even if the connection was dropped, the game will restart with the same ID, and the players will be able to return to the game)
- The Auction should now work as intended;
- The answering player can type in their answer and press the button. The answer will be voiced over with TTS (Text-to-Speech); (Credits: BEASTMXDE)
- The host now has the ability to kick players while they are still joining; (Credits: BEASTMXDE)
- There is now music played during the final bids;
- Fixed: After everyone answered, the question song kept playing over TTS; (Credits: Bogo)
- Fixed: After the end results, the question song was still playing instead of the answer song/audio; (Credits: Bogo)
- Fixed: The Narcissus achievement now works correctly; (Credits: Bogo)
- Fixed: The 'final round' text is now being properly displayed on the game board. (Credits: Bogo)

The 0.5 update is now live! Here's the list of changes:

Gameplay

-    Most of the achievements will no longer be triggered when there are fewer than 3 people playing;
-    When the time to answer a question is almost up and no one has pressed a button yet, a short beeping sound is played;
-    When the time for a player to answer a question is up, the host announces it using text-to-speech (TTS);
-    If a menu dropdown is active and the user presses the Escape button, the dropdown now closes first, before closing the active window;
-    If a question contains both a picture and text, the picture will display for 1.5 seconds before the text appears.

Constructor

-    Fixed an issue with the index of a new round (ROUND X), where X was calculated incorrectly;
-    Fixed an issue where the upload window showed 75% progress initially when uploading a pack to Steam;
-    Fixed the layout of the THEME NAME placeholder.

Misc

-    A credits section is now available from the main menu. Take a moment to look at the list of players who made this game possible.

Enjoy the update and stay tuned for future updates!
